{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012Neu8fEzh7itEdbospq1sh","type":"tool_result","content":"package roles\n\nimport (\n\t\"io/fs\"\n\t\"os\"\n\t\"path\"\n\t\"slices\"\n\t\"sort\"\n\t\"strings\"\n\t\"testing\"\n\t\"testing/fstest\"\n\t\"time\"\n\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/config\"\n)\n\nfunc TestFSContents(t *testing.T) {\n\tvar got []string\n\terr := fs.WalkDir(FS, \".\", func(p string, d fs.DirEntry, err error) error {\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn err\n\t\t}\n\t\tif !d.IsDir() {\n\t\t\tgot = append(got, p)\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn nil\n\t})\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n\t}\n\tsort.Strings(got)\n\twant := []string{\"config.yaml\", \"reviewers/eng-review/prompt.txt\", \"reviewers/license-review/allowlist.txt\", \"reviewers/license-review/prompt.txt\", \"reviewers/security-review/prompt.txt\", \"scanners/cve/Dockerfile\", \"scanners/cve/merge.jq\", \"scanners/cve/scan\", \"scanners/docs/Dockerfile\", \"scanners/docs/docscan.go\", \"scanners/docs/scan\", \"scanners/error-codes/Dockerfile\", \"scanners/error-codes/errcodes.jq\", \"scanners/error-codes/scan\", \"triage/engineer/prompt.txt\", \"triage/lead/prompt.txt\", \"workers/engineer/prompt.txt\"}\n\tif strings.Join(got, \",\") != strings.Join(want, \",\") {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"embedded files = %v, want %v\", got, want)\n\t}\n\tfor _, p := range got {\n\t\tif strings.HasSuffix(p, \"_test.go\") || strings.Contains(p, \"testdata\") {\n\t\t\tt.Errorf(\"%s must not be embedded: ard init would copy it into target repos\", p)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n}\n\n// embed.FS reports 0444 for everything, so the exec bit must be checked on disk\n// to catch a mode lost in git.\nfunc TestScanIsExecutableOnDisk(t *testing.T) {\n\tfor _, p := range []string{\"scanners/cve/scan\", \"scanners/docs/scan\", \"scanners/error-codes/scan\"} {\n\t\tfi, err := os.Stat(p)\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n\t\t}\n\t\tif fi.Mode()&0o111 == 0 {\n\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"%s mode %v has no exec bit\", p, fi.Mode())\n\t\t}\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc TestExecutableNames(t *testing.T) {\n\tif len(ExecutableNames) != 1 || ExecutableNames[0] != \"scan\" {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"ExecutableNames = %v\", ExecutableNames)\n\t}\n}\n\n// This is what #27's writer must do: embed.FS drops modes (everything is 0444),\n// so files named in ExecutableNames are written 0755.\nfunc TestEmbeddedCveRoleLoadsAsScanner(t *testing.T) {\n\t// Without the chmod, config rejects the role: the exec bit really is needed.\n\tif _, err := config.LoadFS(starterFS(t, false), \"/repo\"); err == nil || !strings.Contains(err.Error(), \"executable\") {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"want an 'executable' error without chmod, got %v\", err)\n\t}\n\n# ard configuration, proposed by `ard init`. Edit freely; this file is yours.\n# Anything unset takes its built-in default (docs/proposal.md, Configuration).\n# Validate with `ard config check`. ard serve reads this file from origin/main.\n\n# label: only issues a maintainer labels for triage enter the pipeline.\n# all: every human-filed issue enters.\nintake: { mode: label }\n\nmerge:\n  # A PR touching any of these waits for a human approval. There is no\n  # built-in list: removing an entry removes its gate. An entry ending in /\n  # is a directory prefix; anything else is a glob (quote globs starting with *).\n  protected_paths:\n    - .github/\n    - .ard/config.yaml\n    - .ard/scanners/\n    - .ard/triage/\n    - .ard/workers/\n    - .ard/reviewers/\n    - \"**/CODEOWNERS\"\n    # Agent instructions a PR could plant to steer later agents.\n    - CLAUDE.md\n    - \"**/CLAUDE.md\"\n    - AGENTS.md\n    - \"**/AGENTS.md\"\n    - .claude/\n    - .mcp.json\n\noverrides:\n  scanners/cve: { every: 6h, max_open: 10, group_size: 1, autoclose: true }\n  scanners/docs: { every: 3d, max_open: 3, group_size: 10, autoclose: true }\n  scanners/error-codes: { every: 24h, group_size: 20, autoclose: true }\n  triage/lead:  { model: claude-opus-5-5, timeout: 15m }\n  triage/engineer: { model: claude-sonnet-5-5 }\n  # timeout covers the whole worker job (agent, tests, fix rounds). tests is your\n  # repo's test command; \"\" turns the test step off. Over diff_warn_lines changed\n  # lines the PR goes ahead with a \"Large change\" note; over diff_max_lines it is\n  # held for a human.\n  workers/engineer: { model: claude-sonnet-5-5, timeout: 60m, tests: make test, diff_warn_lines: 1000, diff_max_lines: 2000 }\n  reviewers/eng-review: { model: claude-sonnet-5-5 }\n  reviewers/security-review: { model: claude-opus-5-5 }\n  # Runs only when a dependency manifest or lockfile changes. allowlist.txt in\n  # its directory (or a sidecar's licenses/allowlist.txt) is the license policy.\n  reviewers/license-review: { model: claude-sonnet-5-5, when: { paths: [\"**/go.mod\", \"**/go.sum\", \"**/package.json\", \"**/package-lock.json\", \"**/npm-shrinkwrap.json\"] } }\n     Say what it waits for.\n4. When the status is done, choose:\n   - worker: exactly one name from .ard/workers/. Prefer engineer when it\n     exists.\n   - next: the triage roles whose section the plan needs. Order does not\n     matter; the configuration decides the order. Typical routing, applied\n     only to roles that exist:\n     - engineer: every issue that will reach a worker.\n     - product-manager: a new feature or a change in user-visible behaviour.\n     - architect: a change across several modules or packages, a new\n       dependency or a major-version upgrade, a new public interface, or a\n       change to stored data.\n     - designer: a change to a user interface.\n     - documentation-planner: a change to a public API, the command line, the\n       configuration or documented behaviour.\n     A scanner finding with a narrow fix, such as a patch-level dependency\n     upgrade, usually needs only engineer.\n     Every reviewer runs on every pull request unless .ard/config.yaml gives\n     it a when: rule. Add review:<name> only for such a reviewer whose rule\n     would skip this change although the change needs that review.\n5. Write .ard/N/triage-lead.md.\npackage roles\n\nimport (\n\t\"strings\"\n\t\"testing\"\n\t\"time\"\n\t\"unicode/utf8\"\n\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/agent\"\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/closeout\"\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/config\"\n\t\"github.com/albertcbrown/ard/internal/labels\"\n)\n\nconst engineerPromptPath = \"triage/engineer/prompt.txt\"\n\nfunc TestEmbeddedEngineerLoadsAsTriage(t *testing.T) {\n\tres, err := config.LoadFS(starterFS(t, true), \"/repo\")\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"LoadFS: %v\", err)\n\t}\n\tr, ok := res.Role(config.KindTriage, \"engineer\")\n\tif !ok {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"no triage role engineer in %+v\", res.Roles)\n\t}\n\tif r.PromptPath != \".ard/triage/engineer/prompt.txt\" || r.Dockerfile != \"\" || r.Extra != nil || r.ScanPath != \"\" || len(r.After) != 0 {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"unexpected role: %+v\", r)\n\t}\n\tif r.Model != \"claude-sonnet-5-5\" || r.Timeout != 30*time.Minute || r.Agent != \"claude\" {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"model=%q timeout=%v agent=%q\", r.Model, r.Timeout, r.Agent)\n\t}\n\t// Accepted under #84: no Dockerfile, so the engineer runs as a host\n\t// subprocess. Adding a Dockerfile is a deliberate test change.\n\tfound := false\n\tfor _, h := range res.HostUntrusted() {\n\t\tfound = found || (h.Kind == config.KindTriage && h.Name == \"engineer\")\n\t}\n\tif !found {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"HostUntrusted = %v, want it to include triage/engineer\", res.HostUntrusted())\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc TestEngineerPromptShape(t *testing.T) {\n\tb, err := FS.ReadFile(engineerPromptPath)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n\t}\n\tif !utf8.Valid(b) || len(b) > 16<<10 {\n\t\tt.Fatalf(\"prompt: valid=%v size=%d\", utf8.Valid(b), len(b))\n\t}\n\tfor i, c := range b {\n\t\tif c > 0x7f {\n\t\t\tt.Fatalf(\"non-ASCII byte at %d\", i)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tp := string(b)\n\tfor _, want := range []string{\n\t\tstrings.Replace(agent.RoleFilePath(7, \"triage\", \"engineer\"), \"/7/\", \"/N/\", 1),\n\t\t\".ard-input/N/issue.md\", \".ard-input/N/comments.md\", \".ard/N/plan.md\",\n\t\t\"role: engineer\", \"attempt: 1\", \"UNTRUSTED\",\n146:var starterTree = []string{\".ard/config.yaml\", \".ard/reviewers/eng-review/prompt.txt\", \".ard/reviewers/license-review/allowlist.txt\", \".ard/reviewers/license-review/prompt.txt\", \".ard/reviewers/security-review/prompt.txt\", \".ard/scanners/cve/Dockerfile\", \".ard/scanners/cve/merge.jq\", \".ard/scanners/cve/scan\", \".ard/scanners/docs/Dockerfile\", \".ard/scanners/docs/docscan.go\", \".ard/scanners/docs/scan\", \".ard/scanners/error-codes/Dockerfile\", \".ard/scanners/error-codes/errcodes.jq\", \".ard/scanners/error-codes/scan\", \".ard/triage/engineer/prompt.txt\", \".ard/triage/lead/prompt.txt\", \".ard/workers/engineer/prompt.txt\"}\n201:\tfor _, s := range []string{\"bot-commits.yml\", \"ARD_BOT_LOGIN\", \"Squash and merge\", \".ard/scanners/cve/scan\", \".ard/scanners/error-codes/Dockerfile\", \".ard/scanners/error-codes/errcodes.jq\", \".ard/scanners/error-codes/scan\", \".ard/triage/lead/prompt.txt\", \".ard/triage/engineer/prompt.txt\", \".ard/workers/engineer/prompt.txt\", \".ard/reviewers/eng-review/prompt.txt\", \".ard/reviewers/security-review/prompt.txt\"} {\n231:\tfor _, want := range []string{labels.Running(labels.StageTriage, \"lead\"), labels.Done(labels.StageTriage, \"lead\"), \"ard:triage:engineer\", labels.Running(labels.StageTriage, \"engineer\"), labels.Done(labels.StageTriage, \"engineer\"), labels.Request(labels.StageWorker, \"engineer\"), labels.Running(labels.StageWorker, \"engineer\"), labels.Done(labels.StageWorker, \"engineer\"), labels.Request(labels.StageReview, \"eng-review\"), labels.Running(labels.StageReview, \"eng-review\"), labels.Done(labels.StageReview, \"eng-review\"), labels.Changes(\"eng-review\"), labels.Request(labels.StageReview, \"security-review\"), labels.Running(labels.StageReview, \"security-review\"), labels.Done(labels.StageReview, \"security-review\"), labels.C